  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Engraved Score",
    "overview": "A talk is a performance read like a conductor's score: tempo, rests and dynamics marked against time. The app is set like a well-engraved orchestral part. A deep score-navy rail holds the instrument list (the navigation); the main sheet is cool paper with a faint blue cast, ruled in hairlines, printed in ink. Information is dense and exact, the way a score is: tabular figures, small radii, no ornament that does not mean something.\n\nThe world refuses the category default of grey cards with a blue button and a gamified confetti layer. There is one action color (conductor blue), one reward color (brass, rationed to things the speaker earned), and one decorative voice (the bold italic serif tempo marking). Everything else is ink on paper. Musical notation is the native visual language, not a theme applied on top: sessions are staves, issues are note heads on their category's line, weekly goals are a measure of beats, pauses are breath marks, caesuras and fermatas, and pace is named Adagio to Presto.\n\nThe whole system runs on system fonts and inline SVG. Nothing is downloaded at runtime, light and dark follow the OS, and the same score reads in English, German and right-to-left Urdu.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Navy score rail, paper sheet, ink text; hairline borders instead of shadows.",
      "Conductor blue marks actions and the current place, and nothing else.",
      "Brass appears only on earned things: met weekly measures, streak days, earned achievements.",
      "Notation as data: staves, bar lines, note heads, ties, breath marks and tempo words carry real values.",
      "Bold italic serif tempo markings are the only display voice; all other type is the system sans with tabular figures.",
      "System font stacks only, including Nastaliq for Urdu text and Naskh for Urdu form controls."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Earned Brass Rule",
        "body": "Brass marks only something the speaker achieved (a met goal, a practiced day, an earned badge). It is never an accent, a warning, a hover or a highlight.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Baton Rule",
        "body": "Conductor blue is the only action and current-place color. Selected state is a solid blue fill with white text; idle state is ink on sheet with a rule border. No second action hue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Staff Stays on the Staff Rule",
        "body": "Category hues belong to issue marks on the stave, its legend and transcript highlights. They never color buttons, headings or panels.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Figure Rule",
        "body": "Every number that can change or be compared (scores, words per minute, counts, times, table cells) is set with tabular figures.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Single Marking Voice Rule",
        "body": "The tempo serif is reserved for musical markings and the streak count. Headings, buttons and labels are always the sans.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Script Fits the Control Rule",
        "body": "Urdu text is set in Nastaliq at line height 1.9; Urdu inputs and selects switch to Naskh at line height 1.3 so one-line controls fit. Mono and tabular spans fall back to the sans in Urdu. All are system faces; none is fetched.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hairline-Not-Shadow Rule",
        "body": "Panels separate from paper by a 1px hairline border and a white sheet, never by a drop shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** draw time-based data as notation: staves, bar lines, note heads, ties and tempo words, each carrying a real value.",
      "**Do** keep conductor blue for actions, selection, links, focus and the current place.",
      "**Do** keep brass for things the speaker earned and nothing else.",
      "**Do** separate panels with a 1px hairline on a sheet over paper, 10px corners.",
      "**Do** set every comparable number in tabular figures and every tempo marking in the bold italic serif.",
      "**Do** use system font stacks only, with Nastaliq for Urdu text and Naskh for Urdu controls.",
      "**Do** pin charts, staves, gauges and number groups left-to-right inside right-to-left layouts.",
      "**Do** follow the OS for light and dark, and stop decorative animation under reduced motion."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use drop shadows to lift cards or panels.",
      "**Don't** add a gamified confetti layer, or use brass, amber or category hues as general decoration.",
      "**Don't** introduce a second action color or color buttons with category hues.",
      "**Don't** set headings, buttons or labels in the tempo serif.",
      "**Don't** fetch fonts, icons or images at runtime, or pull in an icon package.",
      "**Don't** set Urdu form controls in Nastaliq; it overflows one-line fields."
    ]
  }
}